 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "West Wind, bring to us a delicate re\nStair-by-stair of winds that come and away\nTo blind and to wash the lids of shadow,\nThat sweetly follow our sorrow.\nThe water heaves with the shadow\nAs it comes and goes and dies or roses\nOf another day that forget\nHave met this same waxed sunset\nOver some barren hill's lone tower. We\nAnd he alone are sorrowfully free\nBecause we have him by shadow.\nThere shall he move as sorrow",
